  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Let Me Bathe in Demonic Light** (1 other source): Crew member Ben played bass, noted alongside this song [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **See America Right**: with Brandon Eggleston! [2]\n- **Let Me Bathe in Demonic Light**: back after 69 archived shows (688 days) [2]\n- **No Children intro (I Hope You Dance)**: rare: 5 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tMG2024-08-10** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 19 songs; 92 min [1]. Said about its sound: Soundboard had to be mixed down to mono, and mic placement relative to the leftmost speaker stack was poor, so listening is sometimes rough [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Guests: Brandon Eggleston! [1]\n- With Peter Hughes recovering from covid and Isa Burke otherwise committed, the band appeared as a surprise trio: John Darnielle, Matt Douglas and Jon Wurster [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tMG2024-08-10**: taped by LMGBTapes; transferred by LMGBTapes; source: CA-14 omnis > CA-Ugly 2 preamp > Sony PCM-10 (on stage, healy) + SBD [Engineer: Brandon Eggleston] > Sony PCM-A10 [1]",
